# Copy to .env.local. Never commit .env.local.

# --- Supabase (required for auth and the synced profile; see docs/SETUP-CLOUD.md) ---
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon key from Project Settings → API>

# Service-role key: scripts/collectors/** only (staging writes bypass RLS). NEVER expose it to
# the browser — nothing under src/ may read it.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<service role key>

# --- Local verification bed (scripts/db/local/up.sh prints this) ---
# Used by npm run test:rls, gen:types, and scripts/db/local/dump-diff.sh. Not read by the app.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:pg@127.0.0.1:54329/macote

# --- Local development WITHOUT a Supabase project ---
# Point the URL at a port nothing listens on so createClient() succeeds and every auth/DB
# call fails fast; the app then runs as a guest (funnel works, outbox stays pending). The
# bypass lets src/proxy.ts serve the protected pages to that guest so `npm run shots` can
# render them against a seeded localStorage profile. Compiled out of production builds.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:1
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=local-dummy
# MACOTE_DEV_AUTH_BYPASS=1

# --- Optional: the public site URL (auth redirects, sitemap, metadataBase). Defaults to https://www.macote.xyz; trailing slash is stripped. ---
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Published page text (src/lib/site-config.ts SITE_CONFIG). Each is optional; an unset one renders a visible
# "à confirmer" chip on the page instead of an invented value. NEXT_PUBLIC_ on purpose: page text, not secrets. ---
# Address shown on /contact and named on /confidentialite and /accessibilite for privacy/accessibility/deletion requests.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL=
# Address the /pour-les-cegeps pilot form mails to (submit stays disabled until set).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PILOT_EMAIL=
# Name and title of the person responsible for the protection of personal information (Loi 25) — /confidentialite.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVACY_OFFICER=
# Where student data is physically hosted, e.g. the Supabase region — /confidentialite hosting sentences.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DATA_REGION=
# Founder's name — /a-propos identity card.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FOUNDER_NAME=
# Founder's cégep — /a-propos identity card.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FOUNDER_CEGEP=

# --- Web Push (optional, not yet wired end to end) ---
# The service worker (src/app/sw.ts) already shows a pushed reminder and handles taps, and the
# /~offline fallback and per-deploy cache version are live. The client subscription UI, the
# settings toggle and the cron sender (scripts/notifications/send-due.ts) are a follow-up; see
# the "Web Push" section in docs/SETUP-CLOUD.md. Generate a pair once with
# `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`: the public half ships to the browser, the private half
# never does.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# Private VAPID key: the cron sender only. Never NEXT_PUBLIC_, nothing under src/ may read it.
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# Contact the push services may use, mailto: or https: (scripts only).
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.com
